.TH SEQ 1
.SH NAME
seq \- print sequences of numbers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seq
[
.I first
[
.I incr
]
]
.I last
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Seq
prints a sequence of integers, one per line, from
.I first
(default 1) to as near
.I last
as possible, in increments of
.I incr
(default 1).
The loop is:
.IP
.EX
for(val = first; val <= last; val += incr) print val;
.EE
.PP
When
.I incr
is negative the sequence counts down and stops at the first value below
.IR last .
An
.I incr
of zero is an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B seq 3
Print
.B "1 2 3"
(on separate lines).
.TP
.B seq 10 -2 4
Print
.BR "10 8 6 4" .
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/seq/main.odin
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B usage
when an argument is not an integer, there are none, or there are more
than three.
.SH BUGS
The numbers are integers.
There is no
.B \-w
and no
.BR \-f .
